               <msContents>
                  <summary>The manuscript contains the following texts (cp. EMML 1495):&#xD; I)
                     ʾAmmǝstu ʾaʿmāda mǝśṭir “The Five Pillars of Mystery" (fols. 1r-11r;
                     69r-126v)&#xD; I-1) Introduction (fols. 1r-3r)&#xD; 
                     I-2) Mǝśṭira Śǝllāse
                     “Mystery of the Trinity” (fols. 3v-11r), including &#xD; II) Maṣḥafa śǝnä fǝṭrat "Book of the Beauty of
                     Creation" (fols. 11r-69r)&#xD;&#xD; I-3) Mǝśṭira śǝggāwe “Mystery of the Incarnation” (69r-104r)&#xD;
                     I-4) Mǝśṭira ṭǝmqat “Mystery of Baptism” (fols. 104r-111r)&#xD; I-5) Mǝśṭira
                     qʷǝrbān “Mystery of the Eucharist” (fols. 111r-119r)&#xD; I-6) Mǝśṭira tǝnśāʾe
                     mutān “Mystery of the Resurrection of the Dead” (fols. 119r-124v)&#xD; I-7)
                     Conclusion: authenticity of this teaching (fols. 124v-125r)&#xD; I-8) Treatise
                     on the birth of Jesus (fols. 125v-126v)&#xD; III) Nagara hāymānot “Discourse on
                     Faith” (fols. 127r-128v), incomplete&#xD; IV) Christian interpretation of
                     Moses’ life (?) (129r-132v), unidentified&#xD; &#xD; Additiones 1-2.</summary>
                 
